      "representation": "verbal",
      "prompt": "For $y={{m}}x{{b|signed}}$, a student says “the zero is {{b}} because {{b}} is the y-intercept.” Correct the student by giving the actual zero and the y-intercept.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "zero",
          "label": "Zero (x-value where y=0)",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "{{root}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "yint",
          "label": "y-intercept",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "{{b}}"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "A zero is an x-value; a y-intercept is an output when x=0.",
        "reasoning": [
          "Setting y=0 gives $0={{m}}x{{b|signed}}$, so the zero is x={{root}}.",
          "Setting x=0 gives y={{b}}, so {{b}} is the y-intercept, not the zero."
        ]
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Decide which coordinate is forced to 0 for each kind of intercept."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "x-intercept/zero: y=0. y-intercept: x=0."
